{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":23778755,"ns":0,"title":"Bioactive paper","extract":"Bioactive paper is a paper-based sensor that can identify various contaminants in food and water. First developed in 2009, bioactive paper research has been ongoing and in 2011 was awarded a 5-year grant totalling $7.5 million CAD. It has been developed at the biosensor stage level, which means it can detect pesticides but is not yet able to repel and deactivate toxins.","description":"Paper treated to react to contaminants","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}